## Control {{controlId}}: Control and Monitor User-Installed Software

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization controls and monitors user-installed software within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Intune application management, update ring policies, and detected application monitoring managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if detectedAppsMonitored}}
**Software Monitoring:**
{{detectedAppsCount}} applications detected across managed endpoints are continuously inventoried:
{{#if apps}}
{{#each apps}}
- **{{displayName}}** v{{version}} — Publisher: {{publisher}} — Installed on {{deviceCount}} devices
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

User-installed applications not deployed through Intune are flagged for review. Unauthorized software is remediated per the software compliance procedure.
{{else}}
Application detection and monitoring has not been confirmed.
{{/if}}

{{#if updateRingsConfigured}}
**Patch Management:**
{{updateRingsCount}} Windows Update ring policies manage software updates and patches:
{{#if rings}}
{{#each rings}}
- **{{displayName}}** — Deferral: {{deploymentDeferralInDays}} days — Update mode: {{automaticUpdateMode}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Update rings enforce timely patching while allowing controlled rollout through deferral periods for testing.
{{else}}
Windows Update ring policies have not been configured. Patch management enforcement is not verified.
{{/if}}

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
**Installation Restrictions:**
Device configuration policies restrict standard users from installing software without administrator approval. Local administrator privileges are removed from standard user accounts to prevent unauthorized software installation.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine detected application reports, update ring configurations, software installation restriction policies, and user software compliance audit logs.

